[
  {
    "_comment": "Medallion-suite descriptor consumed by ../suite.py. One full medallion pipeline per source system (mysql, postgres, oracle, db2, mssqlserver, databricks) over that system's 'bronze' arrival-pattern model (a dedicated table per pattern, a data_ts event timestamp, a (tenant_id, entity_id) business key). Functions are organized on disk by source, then layer, then pattern: functions/<sys>/<layer>/<pattern>.py. Collections mirror the layers, each in its own group: <sys>_src (sources), <sys>_bronze, <sys>_silver, <sys>_gold; the bronze/silver/gold groups are created by ../suite.py at create-project time. Tables are referenced cross-collection between layers (<collection>/<table>@<version>) and bare within a layer. The bronze/silver/gold transformer logic is identical across systems (pure TableFrame helpers); only publishers (Src type + dialect SQL) differ -- the update-stream incremental watermark uses each dialect's epoch expression, and Oracle/Db2 alias SELECT columns to quoted lowercase (they upper-fold unquoted identifiers). Chains per system: append-only, periodic-snapshot, snapshot-diff -> SCD2+SCD1 (entity_* tables), update-stream, and gold Type1/Type2 dims + a fact. CDC-capable systems (mysql, postgres, db2) add a CDC chain: a bootstrap-snapshot publisher (SQL src, in <sys>_src) + a binlog/WAL stream publisher (@stream_publisher via the CDC src, in a dedicated <sys>_cdc_src collection with the *_cdc.yaml connection) -> build_cdc_bronze -> SCD2+SCD1 silver, all under a cdc_* slug so it never collides with the snapshot-diff entity_* tables. Only batch publishers are triggered (detached), including the CDC bootstrap; the continuous CDC stream publisher is registered but started separately. Transformers fire via table dependency (@NEW). NOTE: a single static onboarding load commits everything as inserts, so it populates the bronze/silver tables and the Type1 dims; Type2 history, the fact, and live CDC events become meaningful once the source evolves. GOLD SERVING: the dest layer is split per destination system into functions/<sys>/dest/databricks/<pattern>.py and functions/<sys>/dest/snowflake/<pattern>.py -- one subscriber per (system, pattern), each forwarding that pattern's gold table(s) to <sys>_<table>. Databricks subscribers register in the databricks_dest collection (databricks_bulk_out.yaml, domain databricks_bronze_xs); Snowflake subscribers register in snowflake_dest (snowflake_bulk_out.yaml, domain snowflake). Both serve every system; targets are unique within each destination collection. Each sink fires on <sys>_in_gold/<table>@NEW, so no explicit trigger is needed. Snowflake has no source connector, so it appears only as this gold destination."
  },
